Personality sym91 (Symbian 9.1 user sides, N73) on our kernel (personalities/sym91/README.md):
- its exec tables (personalities/sym91/exec.map: 9.2's numbering cut to 9.1's range; shims for the TLS
  calls, the TInt find handle and LockedInc/LockedDec as fast execs on ARMv5),
  next to 9.2's in the kernel, chosen at boot from the ROM header's personality number;
- the 9.1 loader structure layout (TCodeSegCreateInfo without the demand-paging fields), measured in
  the N73's own ekern: per-personality copy-in/out replaces the 9.2-only TProcessCreateInfo shrink;
- the 9.1 SWI return convention: EUSER stubs are "mov ip, lr; swi n" and the 9.1 kernel returned
  to user mode through "bx ip", so user-mode SWIs return to ip (Thumb if odd);
- CodeSegReadExportDir from ordinal 1 (moving model): the 9.1 loader indexes buf[ordinal-1].

